Source: alderpointdns
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Alderpoint DNS Maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-python, python3

Package: alderpointdns
Architecture: all
Depends: bind9, bind9-dnsutils, curl, dnsdist (>= 1.9.0), gnupg, jq,
 knot-dnsutils, openssl, python3-aioquic, python3-argon2, python3-dnspython,
 python3-fastapi, python3-httpx, python3-itsdangerous, python3-jinja2,
 python3-pip, python3-python-multipart, python3-openpyxl, python3-yaml,
 sqlite3, sudo, uvicorn, ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}
# python3-pip is required at *install/upgrade* time, not just runtime:
# postinst's vendor-deps-sync step (sync_vendored_python_deps() in
# app/alderpointdns_compiler.py) runs `python3 -B -m pip install
# --no-index --find-links vendor/ --target vendor-runtime/ ...` to install
# the pinned python-multipart 0.0.31 wheel ahead of whatever Debian's own
# archive carries. Without this Depends, a stock Debian 13 install
# resolves the package's other dependencies fine, dpkg unpacks the
# files, and postinst then fails outright because `python3 -m pip`
# does not exist -- caught by tests/test_clean_install_container.sh
# against a genuinely clean container, not by any unit test (every
# in-repo unit test runs on a dev machine that already has pip).
# python3-multipart is a DIFFERENT, unrelated Debian package (Andrew
# Dunham's "multipart", currently 1.2.1) that happens to also install as
# `import multipart` -- not the FastAPI-ecosystem "python-multipart"
# dependency this application actually needs (Debian package
# python3-python-multipart, PyPI python-multipart, vendored at a newer
# pinned version -- see app/alderpointdns_compiler.py's
# sync_vendored_python_deps()). If both are ever installed side by side,
# python-multipart's own back-compat shim (multipart/__init__.py) can
# silently prefer whichever bare multipart.py it finds first on
# sys.path, which may be the wrong, incompatible one. Depending on the
# correct package name is the actual fix for fresh installs. Do NOT add
# `Conflicts: python3-multipart` here: python3-python-multipart itself
# declares `Provides: python3-multipart` (a documented Debian rename
# transition), so a Conflicts on that name also conflicts with the
# correct package and makes this package entirely uninstallable --
# confirmed the hard way via a real `dpkg -i` against Debian 13 during
# this fix ("alderpointdns conflicts with python3-multipart /
# python3-python-multipart provides python3-multipart and is present").
# An install that already has the wrong package present is unaffected
# either way: Starlette tries `import python_multipart as multipart`
# first and only falls back to the ambiguous `import multipart` if that
# fails, and the vendored python_multipart wheel above is always present,
# so the fallback path (where the wrong package could actually matter) is
# never reached in practice.
Description: Private DNS filtering and administration appliance
 Alderpoint DNS combines BIND, dnsdist, local DNS records, filtering policy,
 analytics, backup/restore, replication, and encrypted DNS listener controls
 behind a local administration interface.
